From: zyi
Subject: [PATCH] dram: fall back to built-in zero3w DRAM parameters

Our boot flow never populates the /dram node of the FDT the SCP reads
(boot0 wants a dedicated "dtb" item in the boot package and errors out:
"error: dtb not found for scp"; BL31 hands the SCP the kernel DTB at
0x44000000, which has no dram_paraXX unless kernel patch 0030 is in).
Every dram_para00..159 parses to 0, so dram_power_save_process ran with
a null parameter set: the debug SCP console went silent right after
"the first time ddr standby" and the board never came back (deep
suspend hang of 09-29/30).

Fill the array from a built-in table when the parse yields all zeros.
The table is the parameter set boot0 itself trains with: the Orange Pi
Zero 3W carries 4 GiB LPDDR5, and boot0_sdcard_orangepizero3w.fex picks
its header set ("vaild para:4  select dram para0", "DRAM Type =9"),
copied word for word from boot0 offset 0x38, with dram_para2 replaced by
boot0's post-autoscan value (the 4 GiB size field: "para2 = 10001001";
para1 a0fa and tpr13 0x65 are unchanged by the scan).

An earlier version of this table was built from the generic
sys_config.fex [dram_para] block, which is LPDDR4 (type 8) with LPDDR4
drive/MR/timing values: the restore then brought the controller up as
LPDDR4, the SCP read BL31 and the kernel text back as all zeros, and
CPU0 powered up at the BL31 resume entry into nothing (board test
2026-10-01, debug build "dram sum bl31 899B65D3 -> 0").

Index -> field mapping is __dram_para_t (include/driver/dram.h).

--- a/ar100s/driver/dram/dram_dts_para_v2.c
+++ b/ar100s/driver/dram/dram_dts_para_v2.c
@@ -48,6 +48,71 @@ uint32_t *dram_dts_parse(void)
 		printk("dram para[%d] 0x%x\n", i, dts_dram_para[i]);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Zero-para fallback (Orange Pi Zero 3W): our boot flow leaves the
+	 * /dram node of the FDT the SCP reads without any dram_paraXX
+	 * properties, so the whole array parses to 0 and the DRAM
+	 * save/restore would run with a null parameter set (deep suspend
+	 * went silent right after "the first time ddr standby" and never
+	 * woke up). Fill in the parameter set boot0 actually trains with:
+	 * the board has 4 GiB LPDDR5 and boot0_sdcard_orangepizero3w.fex
+	 * selects its header set ("vaild para:4  select dram para0", "DRAM
+	 * Type =9"), copied here word for word. dram_para2 is boot0's
+	 * post-autoscan value ("para2 = 10001001": the 4 GiB size field is
+	 * filled in at runtime, the header carries 0x1001); para1 and tpr13
+	 * are unchanged by the scan ("para1 = a0fa, dram_tpr13 = 65").
+	 *
+	 * The generic sys_config.fex [dram_para] block (LPDDR4, type 8) is
+	 * NOT this board's memory: restoring with it brings the controller
+	 * up as LPDDR4, DRAM reads back as zeros and CPU0 has no BL31 to
+	 * resume into (board test 2026-10-01).
+	 */
+	{
+		static const uint32_t opi_dram_para[32] = {
+			2400,        /* dram_clk */
+			9,           /* dram_type: LPDDR5 */
+			0x0e0e0e0e,  /* dram_dx_odt */
+			0x0f0f0f0f,  /* dram_dx_dri */
+			0xec030e0f,  /* dram_ca_dri */
+			0,           /* dram_para0 */
+			0xa0fa,      /* dram_para1 */
+			0x10001001,  /* dram_para2 (boot0 runtime: + 4 GiB size) */
+			0,           /* dram_mr0 */
+			0,           /* dram_mr1 */
+			0,           /* dram_mr2 */
+			0x6,         /* dram_mr3 */
+			0,           /* dram_mr4 */
+			0,           /* dram_mr5 */
+			0,           /* dram_mr6 */
+			0x14,        /* dram_mr11 */
+			0x44,        /* dram_mr12 */
+			0,           /* dram_mr13 */
+			0x28,        /* dram_mr14 */
+			0,           /* dram_mr16 */
+			0x6,         /* dram_mr17 */
+			0,           /* dram_mr22 */
+			0x4040,      /* dram_tpr0 */
+			0,           /* dram_tpr1 */
+			0x170b0703,  /* dram_tpr2 */
+			0x3800,      /* dram_tpr3 */
+			0x3514,      /* dram_tpr6 */
+			0x325f0000,  /* dram_tpr10 */
+			0,           /* dram_tpr11 */
+			0,           /* dram_tpr12 */
+			0x65,        /* dram_tpr13 */
+			0,           /* dram_tpr14 */
+		};
+		uint32_t any_nonzero = 0;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < 32; i++)
+			any_nonzero |= dts_dram_para[i];
+		if (!any_nonzero) {
+			WRN("dram para all zero -- using built-in zero3w values\n");
+			for (i = 0; i < 32; i++)
+				dts_dram_para[i] = opi_dram_para[i];
+		}
+	}
+
 	dram_para = &dts_dram_para[0];
 
 	return dram_para;
